#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# complex

#% text
# `complex(re, im)` is the complex number `re + im*im`. Arithmetic on `im` builds it, and it prints in this form when its parts are machine reals.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
complex(1, 2)
#% output
#= complex(1, 2)

#% cell
(1 + 2*im)*(3 - im)
#% output
#= complex(5, 5)

#% cell
complex(0.5, 1.5)
#% output
#= complex(0.5, 1.5)

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# Its parts:

#% cell
[re(complex(3, 4)), im_part(complex(3, 4)), abs(complex(3, 4))]
#% output
#= [3, 4, 5]

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `re`, `im_part`, `abs`, `arg`, `conjugate`
